        "title": "Queued prompts stay visible and scroll behaves during streaming",
        "summary": "Two chat fixes land together: auto-follow no longer re-arms itself mid-response, and prompts submitted while a reply is still streaming now render in the transcript with a Queued indicator instead of vanishing until their turn.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Auto-follow now stays off for the rest of a posting session once you scroll up to read — reaching the bottom again (via a late token or layout flush) no longer silently re-engages follow and yanks you back down. A fresh send or explicit jump-to-bottom starts a new follow session.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "00ae87e54ce6ce32f10f17faf9d48c181c77b277"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Prompts submitted while a response is still streaming are now appended to the transcript immediately as queued display messages, rather than only appearing once the previous turn finishes.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "2ab8c6cc600618c798e50edd2ec5399edb63d55a"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "User message bubbles show a subtle \"Queued\" delivery status (with an ARIA status role) while they wait behind the active response, so it's clear the send was accepted.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "2ab8c6cc600618c798e50edd2ec5399edb63d55a"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Chat send now threads a stable clientMessageId through ChatPanel, ChatSurface, and the agent/chat stream hooks so queued prompts keep a consistent identity from submit through delivery.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "2ab8c6cc600618c798e50edd2ec5399edb63d55a"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
        ]
